# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: on a MacBook Air someone docks Notes on the left and Safari on the right. Neither will go as narrow as a
# third of the screen (709 and 574 points, measured on the real apps). They get halves: nothing is kept for the Desktop. A half is seven
# points short for Notes, so Arbor moves the gap itself: both are in view.
# Reference: T03 T20 A05, F61.
# As Arbor ships, what cannot fit overlaps (F69). This story is about the tile, which is an option now.
set windowsThatDoNotFit tile
open Notes 1000x660 min 709x300
open Safari 1324x800 min 574x240
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect left-of 101 102
expect count docked 2
# The first new window of the day floats where it opened, and nothing jumps for it.
open Terminal 585x366
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
# The Desktop has no room, so it shows over the arrangement, in Show Everything too. No docked window becomes a tile for
# the Desktop's sake: somebody has asked for each of them.
zoom 101
show-all
expect visible 103
expect visible 102
expect visible 101
close 103
# Squeezing Safari by hand still makes a tile of it, and Arbor does not push back, now or later.
resize 102 left -150
expect tile 102
zoom 101
back
expect tile 102
expect visible 101
# The hand that squeezed it lets it out again.
resize 102 left 150
expect visible 102
# Whether the Calculator is there before the two are docked makes no difference.
float 101
float 102
open Calculator 230x408
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 104
close 104
# Activity Monitor will not go under 740 points: there is not enough for all three, and the ones docked first are tiles.
open Activity 960x640 min 740x384
dock 105 right
expect visible 105
expect tile 101
expect tile 102
# A click on the tile frames Notes as ever.
zoom 101
expect fills 101
show-all
# Activity Monitor closes: what was taken for it goes back where it came from, and the two have their room again.
close 105
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
# Notes closes: what Safari had lent for its sake goes back to Safari, and what was Notes' own is left over.
close 101
expect visible 102
